x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ and if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431925 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431925 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431925 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431925 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ $3x-1<5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}<4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431925 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4998a63e-08c3-54c9-83d8-95967f9e62e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431925 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-1 & <5 \\\\ 3x & <6 \\\\ x & <2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,2).$\nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=[2,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & <4 \\\\ -2 & <x<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(-2,2)$ \nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [2,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =(-\\infty ,2)\\cap (-2,2) \\\\  & =(-2,2) \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =[2,\\infty )\\cap ((-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [2,\\infty )) \\\\  & =[2,\\infty ) \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(-2,2)\\cup [2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431926 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186431923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431926 #edb/ref 1069 "q-183352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431926 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431926 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ If $x>2,$ then ${x}^{3}>3.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431926 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f523a19-f527-5654-8f5b-d082a72f3c43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431926 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x>2.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{3}>3.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\le 2.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\le 2,$ or ${x}^{3}>3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
